Response: content='North American contractors handle detailed design due to a combination of
industry practices, regulatory frameworks, and project delivery models. Key reasons include:\n\n1.
**Design-Build Delivery Model**: In North America, the design-build project delivery method is
widely used. This model integrates design and construction under a single contract, giving
contractors responsibility for both phases. This allows for greater coordination, faster project
delivery, and improved accountability.\n\n2. **Constructability Expertise**: Contractors possess on-
the-ground knowledge of construction methods, materials, and site constraints. Their involvement in
detailed design ensures that plans are practical, feasible, and optimized for real-world execution,
reducing the risk of delays or rework.\n\n3. **Code Compliance and Safety**: Contractors are
responsible for ensuring that designs meet local, state, and national codes (e.g., NEC, IEEE
standards). Their hands-on experience with compliance requirements helps avoid costly violations and
safety issues during construction.\n\n4. **Subcontractor Coordination**: Contractors manage multiple
subcontractors (e.g., electrical, mechanical, plumbing). Involving them in detailed design ensures
seamless integration of systems and avoids conflicts during installation.\n\n5. **Risk Management**:
By taking ownership of detailed design, contractors assume responsibility for design-related risks,
which aligns with their role in managing project outcomes and liabilities.\n\n6. **Client
Preferences and Market Norms**: Many clients in North America prefer the design-build approach for
its efficiency and single-point accountability. This has become a standard practice, especially in
industrial, commercial, and infrastructure projects.\n\nThese factors are supported by standards
such as IEEE 141 (also known as the IEEE Gold Book), which emphasize the importance of coordination,
detailed engineering, and contractor involvement in design stages—particularly in industrial
substations and electrical systems.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model':
