zigzag transformers used for harmonic current mitigation in power systems.' importance=8\n\n###
Additional Context:\nZigzag transformers (also known as zigzag grounding transformers) are commonly
used in electrical power systems for:\n- Providing a neutral point in ungrounded systems.\n-
Mitigating harmonic currents, especially triplen harmonics (3rd, 9th, 15th, etc.).\n- Enabling
ground fault detection and protection.\n- Supporting grounding in delta-connected systems where no
natural neutral exists.\n\nIn the context of **IEEE standards** like **IEEE Std 493-2007 (Gold
Book)** and **IEEE Std 242 (Buff Book)**, which deal with power system analysis, short-circuit
calculations, and voltage sag analysis, zigzag transformers are relevant for:\n- Harmonic filtering
and mitigation.\n- Improving power quality.\n- Ensuring system stability during faults.\n\nThus,
**ZIYUTEC** is not a company or brand in this context, but rather a technical term referring to
**zigzag transformers** used in power systems for **harmonic current mitigation**."
